{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version "1.12.0"}
        org.clojure/clojurescript {:mvn/version "1.11.132"}
        thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version "2.28.20"}
        ;; The consensus layer, which is **inga**, not engi.
        ;;
        ;; It moved on 2026-08-03 (engi 1f83b16 / ADR-2608038000 D1) and this
        ;; kept pinning the commit before the move — a sha that is still an
        ;; ancestor of engi's main, so nothing broke and nothing said anything.
        ;; The deployed validator was running a consensus layer that no longer
        ;; exists at that address, which meant every fix made in inga was
        ;; invisible here, including the bounded `resume` this pin brings in.
        ;;
        ;; The validator Worker runs inga.replica with torihiki.state as its
        ;; machine; the sequencer Worker does not use it and pays nothing for
        ;; it, since shadow-cljs only compiles what is required. `inga.replica`
        ;; requires consensus / pacemaker / quorum / attest / stake / sync /
        ;; wire and NOT `inga.state`, so arrangement does not reach the bundle.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/inga
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/inga.git"
         :git/sha "28631ff0fc5f4c672913b27955d88dafe0ea5464"}
        ;; The candle fold. The terminal draws from the same library, so
        ;; `/candles` and the chart cannot disagree about what a candle is.
        ;; The IPLD layer: canonical DAG-CBOR and CIDv1. Block identity is a
        ;; CID, so this is on the consensus path, not beside it.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/io-ipld
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/io-ipld.git"
         :git/sha "14b53ae08e0db906355d2ceaa1f9d8288e07f797"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/torihiki-chart
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/torihiki-chart.git"
         :git/sha "80ab3d78ee3896c40d050c025c229be23450e584"}
        ;; main, and the reason it was not main is gone.
        ;;
        ;; This pinned a hotfix branch because main had moved the state
        ;; encoding three times (a governance leaf, `:deficit`, pending
        ;; withdrawals) and I had concluded that advancing to it forks the
        ;; chain: replicas on either side compute different state roots for
        ;; identical state, which is the shape of the divergence the root
        ;; exists to catch.
        ;;
        ;; **That conclusion was wrong.** A block is
        ;; `height / parent-hash / proposals / proposer / ts`
        ;; (`inga.consensus/canonical-block`) and nothing else. It carries no
        ;; state root, `inga.consensus` never mentions one, and
        ;; `inga.replica/state-root` is computed on demand from machine state
        ;; for REPORTING. Consensus orders transactions; it never compares
        ;; what executing them produced.
        ;;
        ;; So an encoding change is an ordinary deploy. Replicas report
        ;; different roots while the rollout is in flight — the window is real
        ;; and visible in `/head` — and converge once all four run the same
        ;; code, which is exactly what was observed when a divergent replica
        ;; restarted onto unified code and replayed.
        ;;
        ;; What this brings live: collateral totals under the root
        ;; (`commit/reserves`), bad debt as `:deficit` rather than a negative
        ;; balance, withdrawals that raise a claim instead of deleting money,
        ;; who may mint committed to the root, liquidation driven by the block
        ;; rather than by a keeper, and cancel-all / amend.
        io.github.kotoba-lang/torihiki
        {:git/url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/torihiki.git"
         :git/sha "ad3e2f49af7bd184cbf0e6f0517078f685fb5f15"}}}
